WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:01.650
- [Kelly] All right, we are back.

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:04.680
And earlier this year I
celebrated my 40th birthday,

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.124
and here on the show,

00:00:06.124 --> 00:00:06.990
(audience cheering)
they went all out.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:08.191
I'm very excited.

00:00:08.191 --> 00:00:09.510
I was surprised though,

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:12.000
with a Mariachi band, margaritas,

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.840
even a giant queso fountain,
which, come on, that's heaven.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:17.880
And I'm not the only one who's gotten

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.920
to party in style on their birthday.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.790
From fine wine, to terrifying
clowns, to giant elephants.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.320
I've heard some amazing stories here

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:26.910
on this stage so take a look.

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.540
You have a big birthday coming up, 30.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:29.402
- I do.
- That's exciting.

00:00:29.402 --> 00:00:30.480
(audience cheering)
- The big 3-0.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:31.634
- 30, 30, 30, y'all.

00:00:31.634 --> 00:00:33.210
(audience cheering)
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:34.110
- [Kelly] Your husband, Chris Pratt,

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:35.820
he had a birthday,
right? A recent birthday.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.290
- Oh, yeah, last week.
- What'd you get him?

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:38.640
- I got him piggies.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.010
'Cause I was told they would
stay small, they did not.

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:43.020
- You had kind of an
LA birthday this year.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.527
- I was like, "Guess what guys,"

00:00:44.527 --> 00:00:46.587
"you're doing cryo for my birthday!"

00:00:47.555 --> 00:00:49.620
- [Machine Gun Kelly] Dave
Chappelle flew us on his jet

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.690
to just chill with him for a night.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:53.917
We landed and he was like,
"Ooh, forgot we gotta go to"

00:00:53.917 --> 00:00:55.769
"my mom's 81st birthday party."

00:00:55.769 --> 00:00:58.860
(audience laughing)

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:00.000
- Did you turn 40 this year?

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:00.833
- I did turn 40.

00:01:00.833 --> 00:01:01.950
- Are you 1979?

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:02.783
- Yes, sir.

00:01:02.783 --> 00:01:04.260
- This is something you
can enjoy this year,

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:05.430
I know you've had an incredible year.

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:07.020
Or you can save it 'til you're 50.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:07.920
- Holy cow.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:09.990
- And for me this is one of
the great wines of the world.

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:10.823
- This is 1979, this is the--

00:01:10.823 --> 00:01:12.510
That'll bring a tear to your eye, no joke.

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:13.649
- Thank you, man.
- That's for real.

00:01:13.649 --> 00:01:14.482
- This is a real--

00:01:14.482 --> 00:01:16.721
- This is one of the most
rare wines of the world.

00:01:16.721 --> 00:01:18.223
(audience clapping)

00:01:18.223 --> 00:01:20.640
- Is this photo from one
of your birthday parties?

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:22.800
'Cause this is, you look terrified.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:24.690
- [Taylor Lautner] See, I don't even

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:27.180
remember where that's from but, yeah,

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:29.789
clearly you can see it
in my eyes. I'm not--

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:32.766
- I will say, Flip Flop the
clown does look scary as hell.

00:01:32.766 --> 00:01:33.690
Like, it's like--
(both laughing)

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:35.490
- I mean, who likes clowns?

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:37.410
- Well, and that one particularly looks

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:39.736
like he might wear your skin.
- Flip Flop is--

00:01:39.736 --> 00:01:41.160
- Yeah. (laughs) Like, he might, yeah.

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:42.672
He looks scary. Like, he
looks kind of scary, yeah.

00:01:42.672 --> 00:01:44.734
- He's a little sketchy.
I do not trust him.

00:01:44.734 --> 00:01:47.130
(audience laughing and clapping)

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:50.460
- During the movie you
celebrated your birthday with,

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.712
is it the mordida? Mordida?
- Yeah.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:53.640
- Is that how you say it? Okay, okay.

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:56.340
- [Salma Hayek] There is a
tradition that we have in Mexico

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:58.830
that, when the cake
comes, you make a wish,

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:01.560
you blow the candle, and
then somebody behind you

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:03.360
whacks you on the head,
- What?

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:05.340
- And puts your face inside of the cake.

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:06.780
- No!
- Very normal in Mexico.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:09.360
And Angie, she just
came to bring me a gift.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:12.420
And when everybody started,
(claps) "Mor-di-da! Mor-"

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:14.010
She's like, "What's happening?"

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:16.200
And I said, "Oh, this is tradition,

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.690
and you're sitting next
to me, so you get to put,

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:22.200
She goes, "I'm not gonna do
that! Are you guys kidding me?"

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.367
I said, "No, no, no, no.
Really, it's a tradition."

00:02:24.367 --> 00:02:26.790
"Somebody whacks you in
the head inside of a cake?"

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:27.676
- It's a weird tradition.

00:02:27.676 --> 00:02:29.356
- And I said, "Yeah,
just do it, it's okay."

00:02:29.356 --> 00:02:30.189
(mimicking Angelina Jolie) "I can't!"

00:02:30.189 --> 00:02:31.050
"Just do it!"

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.180
And all of a sudden
she's like, very girly,

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:34.909
and all of a sudden she goes like, BWOOM!

00:02:34.909 --> 00:02:37.800
(Kelly laughing)
She was worse than Valentina!

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:39.927
And I'm afraid of my daughter
when it comes to the mordida,

00:02:39.927 --> 00:02:41.400
but you know what?

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:42.565
She'll have her birthday coming.

00:02:42.565 --> 00:02:43.398
(audience clapping)
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:43.398 --> 00:02:44.231
- Gonna play the mordida.

00:02:44.231 --> 00:02:45.251
- We'll do the mordida to Angie.

00:02:45.251 --> 00:02:46.260
- You're gonna be sitting' right there.

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:48.380
- Yeah.
- Love that.

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:50.490
- For my 40th birthday, my friends

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:53.445
got me a message from Ken bone.

00:02:53.445 --> 00:02:56.640
Ken bone was the guy, and
I became obsessed with him

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:59.010
for some reason, who in--
- Who is Ken Bone?

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:00.750
- I'm gonna, well, that's
what I'm about to tell you.

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:03.270
So, Ken Bone was the guy,

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:06.930
in like the 2016 election time

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:10.904
there was a debate. And
this one very special man

00:03:10.904 --> 00:03:13.380
from the audience was
wearing this tight sweater,

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:15.570
you guys remember this?
He had like this sweater,

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:17.680
and he just was, he just completely--

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:19.290
- Oh!
- [Josh Gad] Ken Bone!

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:22.020
That's Ken Bone. Thank you to your crew

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:24.480
for showing you Ken Bone.
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:26.220
So, so I became obsessed.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:29.430
So they knew I was obsessed,
and they got him to

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:31.470
deliver a message for my birthday,

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:34.110
and it was just, that was so wonderful.

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:36.696
- I love that you have
met (bursts into laughter)

00:03:36.696 --> 00:03:38.700
so many amazing people.
- Like, Steven Spielberg,

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:39.697
just like, every pop star, and I'm like,

00:03:39.697 --> 00:03:41.215
Ken Bone.
- Ken Bone.

00:03:41.215 --> 00:03:42.665
- Yeah.
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:03:42.665 --> 00:03:44.340
Ken Bone.
- That's amazing.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:46.774
- Barbra Streisand? Yes, I've met her.

00:03:46.774 --> 00:03:49.410
We're talking about Ken Bone.
- Ken Bone? (Kelly cheering)

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.230
- Yeah.
- (laughs) That's amazing.

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:52.543
- Yeah.
(audience clapping)

00:03:52.543 --> 00:03:54.360
- [Howie Mandel] It was her birthday, and

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:56.880
I wanted to surprise my
wife. My wife loves animals.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:58.140
Any kind of animal.
- Me too.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:01.650
- So, I, an elephant.
I rented an elephant.

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:04.110
And I had it brought to the house.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.160
There's the elephant.

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:08.670
And there's my wife.
(audience laughing)

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:11.130
So the next day, the gardener came,

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:12.447
he comes around the corner,

00:04:12.447 --> 00:04:15.630
the yard has these holes
that are 4 feet deep,

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:16.920
the sprinklers are broken,

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:19.410
5 palm trees are laying
all over the place,

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:21.120
and there's a pile of,

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:22.747
and the guy walks in and he goes,

00:04:22.747 --> 00:04:25.770
"Mr. Mandel, what is this?"

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:28.137
And I go, "It was my wife's birthday."

